T-095 — negative control for NextStepPermissionTest
====================================================

The question this answers: does the permission check actually catch a next step
whose door the reader cannot open, or is its green run green because it does
nothing?

Method. A fixture — not a change to ErrorCode.java, which is reserved — was fed
through the same loop the real enum goes through:

    Verdict control = check(new Subject("Reinstate the scrapped equipment.",
            Set.of("equipment"), Set.of("MANAGE_INVENTORY")), model);

Everything about that fixture except the sentence is real and read from the tree:
equipment condition is changed behind MANAGE_INVENTORY (Temple Admin, Kitchen
Manager, Kitchen Staff) and taking a scrapping back is
REINSTATE_SCRAPPED_EQUIPMENT (Temple Admin alone, D-15). It is KMS-400043's real
defect, restated in the permission's own vocabulary so the matcher can see it.

