BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 3s

Outcome. The check named the code and the permission, and named the two roles
that lack it. The injection was then reverted; the fixture survives as the
permanent test "the check catches a next step whose door the reader cannot open",
alongside its positive half ("the same sentence behind the right permission is
left alone") — without which a check that flagged the sentence unconditionally
would also have looked caught.

What this control does NOT establish: that the check would catch KMS-400043
itself. It would not. The real sentence is "Register a replacement, or reinstate
this item if it's back in use.", and REINSTATE_SCRAPPED_EQUIPMENT scores one
matching word against it where two are required. That is the honest gap, and it
is why this control had to be sharpened rather than lifted verbatim.
